    <p class="text-body-lg text-body mb-8">
      Arm pain — especially lateral epicondylitis (tennis elbow), medial epicondylitis (golfer's elbow), and generalized forearm fatigue — is one of the most frequent physical complaints among active pickleball players. In our hands-on court testing with over 45 pickleball paddle setups, we found that equipment specifications directly influence kinetic shock transmission to the arm. In our experience on court, combining <a href="/blog/paddle-weight-guide/" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">paddle weight</a>, <a href="/blog/core-thickness-explained/" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">core thickness</a>, and <a href="/blog/how-to-measure-grip-size/" class="text-link font-medium hover:underline">grip size</a> can reduce peak vibration impact by up to 50%.
    </p>

    <!-- Prominent Medical Disclaimer -->
